      "description": "A hand points to a small black spike covered in brown mud.\nThe fins spine of a Ctenacanth shark was discovered in a section of Mammoth Cave. Ctenacanth sharks are characterized by having pronounced spines right in front of their dorsal fins. These spines were used for deterring predation by larger fish, such as bigger ctenacanth sharks.\nKeywords: Research; Paleontological Resources Inventory; Fossil; Shark Fossil; National Park Service Paleontology Program; Paleontology; Mammoth Cave National Park; Mammoth Cave",
